# The static fields of a class lie in the statics until its class object is made whole, which the first read of a static method does: their values move to properties of the object and the words are emptied.
# The walk believes of that read that it writes nothing that anybody sees, and that holds for as long as compiled code reads such a word anew at every access and takes an empty one to the road by name: the store
# in grow() stands behind a test of its own, behind the read of `tell`, though the same word was read in front of it. The net under effects counted the emptied word as a variable that was given another value.
# RUN: run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 18 function
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(WALK): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# WALK: = GetStaticFieldOrAbsent
# WALK: = PropGet {{*}} key="tell" traits=[mayThrow, mayCollect, mayTouchMemory]
# WALK: = GetStaticFieldOrAbsent
# WALK: = PutStaticField
